            "review_title": "Review at Quán Oc Khanh",
            "review_text": "BL_Leo\nPetaling Jaya, Malaysia4030 contributions\n0\nGrilled seafood Vietnamese style\nApr 2020 • Family\nWe were staying in Somerset Ho Chi Minh and this restaurant was within the walking distance to where we stayed. \"This is where we get to eat good and cheap seafood, Vietnamese style.. and also the way they eat\" said my bro-in-law after a long day sight-seeing around the city area. We stopped by the main road and had to walk through a small alley to reach this restaurant. \n\nIt was packed and we had no choice but to sit right outside the main entrance along the pedestrian walkway (kaki lima in Malay) - same like everyone else, low plastic tables and chairs.\n\nThe modus operandi was to walk to where they display the seafoods, take your pick and let them cook before serving it to you while waiting with, say, few bottles of cold Saigon Export beer. We started with Vietnamese baguette (similar to French because they were colonised by the French in the past).. crispy outer layer and fluffy on the inside. \n\nNeedless to say, the eggs, baby squid, mussels, bamboo clam, grilled squid, grilled snail (edible ones of course), blanched cockles and their stir fried mee topped generously with water spinach and mushrooms were the highlights - in fact the mee finished in the fastest time. For me, I love each and every dish that we'd ordered. \n\nThis is the authentic way to enjoy food the Vietnamese style - I remember my first trip to HCM City not long ago (business trip) and we were also sitting like this by the main road while having seafood in District 5. It was also a good exercise to walk a short distance back to the hotel\nRead more\nWritten April 8, 2020",
            "rating": 5.0,
